  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  HCODX PREVIEW RENDER ENGINE — sbx.hcodx.io/render.html
  VERSION: 5.0.0-render  (was preview.hcodx.io/index.html v4.7.2)
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  CROSS-ORIGIN ISOLATION (v5.0.0):
    This file is the preview RENDER ENGINE. It is served from the dedicated
    render origin (sbx.hcodx.io) and is the ONLY place previewed project code
    executes. Its single trusted controller is the broker shell on
    preview.hcodx.io (PARENT_ORIGIN below). Because project code is now
    cross-origin to both the controller and the editor (hcodx.io), it can no
    longer reach their realms, mutate their DOM, or forge their-origin
    messages — closing the preview-isolation blocker from the editor audit.
    The pipeline below is unchanged from the previous shell; only the trusted
    origins moved. See controller/index.html for the broker and README.md.
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  NEW in v4.7.2:
  ✅ PRO-BRIDGE     Relay the emulator's "pro" bridge messages through the
                    shell in BOTH directions: { source:'hcodx-pro-cmd' } from
                    the emulator is forwarded DOWN to the inner user page, and
                    { source:'hcodx-pro' } from the inner page's capture bridge
                    (e.g. inspect-pick) is forwarded UP to the emulator. The
                    shell previously only switched on HCODX_* message TYPES, so
                    inspect / touch-sim / UA-spoof commands never reached the
                    bridge — the "Inspect button does nothing" bug.

  NEW in v4.7.1:  (CRITICAL — follow-up to 4.7.0)
  ✅ FIX-STALEREV   HTML files are no longer dedup-copied across revisions.
                    rewriteAssetPaths() bakes the current rev into every
                    asset URL at write time; the fileHashMap dedup layer then
                    copied an unchanged HTML file's body verbatim into each
                    new revision — carrying the OLD baked rev in its asset
                    URLs. Once that rev aged out of REV_KEEP, navigating to
                    any page whose HTML was frozen (i.e. any page other than
                    the one currently being edited) 404'd ALL of its assets
                    while the HTML itself still served fine. HTML now always
                    re-encodes (re-rewrites against the current rev). Binary /
                    CSS / JS still dedup — they carry no baked rev. This was
                    latent before 4.7.0 but masked by the old cross-session
                    wipe constantly resetting sessions before revisions could
                    accumulate past 3; removing that wipe surfaced it.

  NEW in v4.7.0:  (CRITICAL — multi-surface cache corruption fix)
  ✅ FIX-XSESSION   Removed the destructive cross-session cache wipe.
                    Every preview surface (split pane, new tab, emulator,
                    lighthouse) shares ONE Service Worker + ONE Cache on
                    preview.hcodx.io, but each shell load minted its own
                    SESSION_ID and, on SW-ready, fired
                    HCODX_SW_PRUNE_OLD_SESSIONS { keepSessionId: <self> }.
                    The SW then deleted EVERY other session's files — so
                    opening a new tab, or a split-pane reboot (triggered by
                    the connector's hard-reload threshold after N edits),
                    wiped the OTHER live surface's cache. Its iframe still
                    pointed at the now-deleted /preview/{oldSession}/… URLs,
                    so the next sub-resource / navigation / reload 404'd
                    until a full page refresh minted a fresh session and
                    re-pushed the files. This was the "all paths become 404
                    after opening a new tab once, or after many edits" bug.
  ✅ OWN-CLEANUP    Each shell now cleans up ONLY ITS OWN session, on real
                    teardown (pagehide with persisted===false → next call is
                    HCODX_SW_CLEAR_SESSION { sessionId: <self> }). A live
                    sibling surface is never touched. bfcache freezes
                    (persisted===true) are skipped so a restored page keeps
                    its cache.
  ✅ BOUNDED-GC     onSwReady now triggers HCODX_SW_DEEP_CLEANUP (count-based,
                    GC_KEY_LIMIT in sw.js) instead of session-nuking. Dead
                    leftovers are reclaimed by total-entry pressure, never by
                    targeting a specific (possibly live) session.
  ✅ FIX-PRUNERACE  pruneOldRevisions() is now trailing-debounced (~400ms).
                    It fired on EVERY write and the SW processes those async
                    (full cache.keys() scan each time); a prune built at rev A
                    could be processed AFTER rev B was written, and since B
                    wasn't in A's keepRevisions snapshot the SW deleted the
                    revision the iframe was CURRENTLY showing — an intermittent
                    404 under fast typing. Debouncing means only the trailing
                    prune fires per burst, always carrying the latest
                    revHistory (which includes the current rev).

  NEW in v4.5.0:
  ✅ EXT-MIME     guessMime() now covers every extension used in
                  modern HTML projects:
                  • Styles:  styl, stylus
                  • Scripts: vue, svelte
                  • Data:    map (source maps), yaml, yml, graphql, gql
                  • Images:  svgz, heic, heif, jxl
                  • Audio:   oga, opus
                  • Video:   ogv, m4v
  ✅ ISTEXT       isText detection extended to recognise text/yaml
                  so YAML files are served with charset=utf-8.
  ✅ ATTR-REWRITE rewriteAssetPaths now handles additional HTML
                  attributes used by lazy-load libraries and legacy
                  markup:
                  • data-bg, data-background, data-original,
                    data-lazy-src, data-image  (lazy-load bg URLs)
                  • data-srcset                (lazy srcset)
                  • data-poster                (lazy video poster)
                  • formaction                 (<button>/<input>)
                  • background                 (<body>/<table> legacy)

  NEW in v4.4.4:
  ✅ FIX-OVERLAY     applyUpdate now re-shows the status overlay at the start
                    of every update cycle (clears display:none + removes the
                    'hidden' class). Previously the overlay stayed permanently
                    invisible after the first hideOverlay() call, causing the
                    old page to linger visibly during cache writes.
  ✅ FIX-BOOT-REUSE  Reverted double-navigation approach. The overlay re-show
                    (FIX-OVERLAY) is sufficient: it masks the iframe while the
                    cache write runs on returning visits. fileHashMap dedup
                    makes returning-visit cache writes fast (copies unchanged
                    files from prev revision instead of re-encoding). One
                    navigation total — no boot frame reset needed.
  ✅ FIX-SPLIT   rewriteAssetPaths split regex now matches BOTH
              </script> and <\/script> (escaped backslash variant
              emitted by CONSOLE_INJECTOR and some frameworks). The
              previous v4.4.0 regex only matched </script>, so the
              injected console block was never captured as a script
              segment — its JS was processed as HTML markup, corrupting
              it and producing "Unexpected token" errors.
  ✅ FIX-ORDER   rewriteAssetPaths now runs on RAW HTML BEFORE
              injectConsoleScript in both the cache-write and boot-frame
              paths. This makes the fix order-independent as a
              belt-and-suspenders measure against any future injector
              changes.
  ✅ FIX-URL     Removed the 'i' flag from the url() rewrite regex so
              it no longer matches JS new URL() / URL() constructors
              in script blocks that might escape the split.

  NEW in v4.4.0 / v4.3.0 / older: (see git history)
